  "master_resume_text": "20+ years in strategic partnerships, business development, consultative account management, market expansion, sales leadership, implementation, customer relationships, training, and business operations. At AO Globe Life, led an end-to-end 90-day pilot that converted territory-based in-home presentations into a virtual operating model using Zoom consultations, electronic signatures, remote client service, onboarding, coaching, communication, and performance practices. The validated model expanded into nationwide remote sales and service. Launched and developed the first Veterans Division over two years, built VFW and AMVETS relationships, created repeatable market-entry and relationship-selling practices, recruited and coached agents, delivered recurring Master Trainings, and influenced broader market specialization through field results and leadership communication. At SeQuential Environmental Services and Mahoney Environmental, managed 5,000+ accounts across Oregon, southwest Washington, and northern California while opening territories, supporting merger activity, and coordinating negotiation, implementation, operations, collections, retention, and ongoing relationships. Exceeded quota four consecutive years and managed relationships with Nike, IKEA, Intel, Daimler, Topgolf, Dave's Killer Bread, and other enterprise customers. At Verizon, led 12 sales professionals and three operations employees, overseeing hiring, onboarding, weekly development, coaching, scheduling, performance, customer experience, and profitability. Consulted with owners and executives of 1-99 employee businesses, translated business needs into practical technology solutions, coordinated implementation and post-sale resources, and proposed a process improvement projected to save approximately $40,000 per month. At CarMax, selected by management to train new hires in customer discovery, consultative sales, objection handling, and the end-to-end sales process. B.S. in Multimedia and Web Design. Practical AI fluency in progress through Google and Anthropic coursework; uses ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini for business research, workflow design, content development, and structured planning. Not a software engineer, AI engineer, deep technical product manager, or hands-on AI/ML builder."
